      "writtenOn": "2024-09-13T13:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d try to open a generic `org.apache.sshd.client.session.ClientSession` against test Gerrit and, after authentication, without sending any command, let it wait until the server closes the connection because the client is idling. Similar to mina-sshd\u0027s KeepAliveTest. I didn\u0027t figure out how to authenticate the session against Gerrit.\n\n```\ntry (ClientChannel channel \u003d session.createChannel(Channel.CHANNEL_SHELL)) {\n    long waitStart \u003d System.currentTimeMillis();\n    Collection\u003cClientChannelEvent\u003e result \u003d channel.waitFor(EnumSet.of(ClientChannelEvent.CLOSED), WAIT);\n    long waitEnd \u003d System.currentTimeMillis();\n    assertTrue(result.containsAll(EnumSet.of(ClientChannelEvent.CLOSED)),\n            \"Wrong channel state after wait of \" + (waitEnd - waitStart) + \" ms: \" + result);\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a207c913_ad4f7bd3",
      "revId": "619adecb4778837dcf1a2ab3cad8b922c1d0c52d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
